# Complete predefined registry Source proposal

This held proposal implements the complete pinned EnergyPlus 26.1
`SetPredefinedTables` registration sequence and its three allocation helpers
plus `addFootNoteSubTable`. It is unapplied and unexecuted. It supplies the
genuine layer-column registry needed by the accepted CTF reportLayers owner;
ordinary Init/backend/report completion and numerical gates remain pending.

`PredefinedRegistry` retains the full allocated reportName, subTable and
columnTag arrays, independent integer capacities and occupied counts, all
1,301 named ID members and the actual pdchOpqConsLayCol vector. The three
record types preserve every Source member. TableEntry, component-size,
shadow and unrelated predefined aggregates remain separate caller owners;
SetPredefinedTables does not touch them.

`set_predefined_tables(&mut self, do_zone_sizing, do_system_sizing)` executes
the whole literal sequence. The catalog contains 19 report calls, 113
subtable calls, 1,053 column calls (including ten real layer-vector pushes),
and 21 footnote calls. All strings, assignment names, parent operands,
call order and the sole sizing conditional were checked against Source.
The sizing branch contains one report, eight subtables and 85 columns.
These are static Source inventories, not expected Native result records.

The complete catalog is a separate Rust include, with one literal call per
Source operation. The member-name include lists each actual declaration.
These large static lists account for most proposal lines; there is no
operation interpreter, generated runtime registry, added dependency or
replacement proof framework.

Default denotes the actual value-initialized registry created by
EnergyPlusData's make_unique<OutputReportPredefinedData>() (or clear_state's
value-initialized replacement). HH has 1,298 explicit zero member
initializers and three AWHP integers without in-class initializers. Those
three are zero in this genuine value-initialization context. Default does
not assert initialized values for arbitrary default-initialized C++ storage.

For unallocated arrays, each original helper allocates 100 records and
resets its capacity/count to 100/1, even when supplied counters were stale.
Allocated arrays increment the real count, double capacity when necessary,
retain old slots and default-construct the new tail. Report creation writes
all four report members and resets show=false. Subtable creation writes only
name/report index, retaining a footnote in an existing next slot. Column
creation writes heading/subtable index. Helpers accept the Source parent
integers without inventing parent-index validation.

Repeated Set calls append real records and ten more layer IDs. Named IDs
assigned on that visit are replaced; skipped sizing IDs retain prior values.
The retained vector is borrowed through opaque_layer_columns()->&[i32] by
the accepted reportLayers function. No hardcoded layer column numbers or
second independent registry are introduced.

Rust representation failures reuse CtfReportUnavailable::TableOwner and
TableCapacity. Missing/extra named members, incompatible allocated shape or
unrepresentable signed arithmetic are unavailable, not invented Native
diagnostics or successful returns. The literal footnote guard ignores
negative/out-of-range indices; Source index zero passes its guard and then
dereferences outside the one-based array. This Rust owner returns unavailable
for that case and makes no full Native behavior claim. Allocation failure
and arbitrary non-one-based imported arrays are outside this fixed owner.

Eight unexecuted tests cover the genuine constructor context, allocation
reset/growth with retained slots, selective member writes, actual catalog
parent/layer associations, either sizing flag, repeated registration and
skipped-ID retention, footnote boundaries and malformed imported owners.
The catalog correspondence JSON records text-only checks, with no execution
of Rust or Original and no endpoint values.

The sole parent edit adds pub mod predefined_tables to actual formatted
backend parent78. Four new module/include/test destinations are absent.
Before bytes equal the immutable actual backend final archive. Another
postlude declaration must be composed through a later actual-parent rebase;
neither proposal may replace the other's declaration.

Ordinary production connection is still required. Native ManageSimulation
calls SetPredefinedTables after real state initialization/checks and before
SetPreConstructionInputParameters. Native GetProjectData resets sizing flags
false, then reads the first actual SimulationControl object and its YES
fields. Current TypedModel/compiler do not retain these sizing flags. A
future ordinary input/state producer must preserve that real default/getter
sequence; this proposal takes the actual flags explicitly and does not force
false. The current postlude will borrow this retained registry's layer IDs
alongside its separate actual table, Scan state and caller-owned sinks.

Genuine Native verification should capture constructor/retained arrays,
counts, capacities, all named IDs and the layer vector before/after complete
Set calls for both sizing conditions and repeated calls, plus the real
reportLayers entries referencing these IDs. No output/hash/count/outcome or
SourceSnapshot is predicted here. Root and an independent full Source peer
must accept this hold before application; later actual comparison is needed
before any registry/report equivalence claim. No canonical, Git, target,
formatter, binary, weather or scientific-result operation was performed.
